  "interpretation": [
    "At32threads the chosen build passes all12 comparisons against actual0.1.0; stack64 improves about15x, denseN4 about10x, denseN16 about2.6x. Larger stack256 and small controls pass unchanged regression limits.",
    "At4threads N16 loses an intermediate stage6 build advantage: final-inline versus stage6 is1.298x, but final-inline versus actual0.1.0 is1.020x and passes the unchanged5percent limit. Stack64 passes its unchanged10percent limit versus actual0.1.0. This intermediate regression remains unresolved and is not hidden.",
    "Read-only source and normalized-assembly inspection found N16 still performs16 products of30x480x30, each selecting4workers. LU scheduling is unchanged. Normalized instructions matched for LocalMatrix::apply_into, InteractionFactor::factorize, Lu::new and closure, gemm and inner closure, and product_into closures. Code placement or runtime behavior remains possible; no demonstrated algorithmic cause.",
    "A temporary <=4-worker exception did not resolve the intermediate regression, so that unearned branch was removed. Its build and all raw measurements are retained.",
    "No memory allocation or pool state added by the scheduling policy. Full Rust/Python CI is owned by the parent task and was not run during these timings. The new unit test still requires that CI pass."
  ],
